{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q276735","formula":"Ag₃N","hill":"Ag3N","elements":["N","Ag"],"composition":{"N":1.0,"Ag":3.0},"names":{"en":"Silver nitride","ru":"Нитрид серебра(I)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Silver nitride is an explosive chemical compound with chemical formula Ag3N. It is a black, metallic-looking solid which is formed when silver oxide or silver nitrate is dissolved in concentrated solutions of ammonia, causing formation of the diammine silver complex which subsequently breaks down to Ag3N. The standard free energy of the compound is about +315 kJ/mol, making it an endothermic compound which decomposes explosively to metallic silver and nitrogen gas.","ru":"Нитрид серебра(I) — неорганическое соединение металла серебра и азота с формулой Ag3N, коричневые кристаллы, плохо растворяется в воде, разлагается со взрывом при нагревании."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Ag+].[Ag+].[Ag+].[N-3]","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-985299","atoms":23,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.927,0.0,0.0],[0.0,3.927,0.0],[0.0,0.0,8.118]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":1.963,"z":2.03,"el":"Ag"},{"x":3.927,"y":1.963,"z":2.03,"el":"Ag"},{"x":1.963,"y":0.0,"z":2.03,"el":"Ag"},{"x":1.963,"y":3.927,"z":2.03,"el":"Ag"},{"x":1.963,"y":1.963,"z":0.0,"el":"Ag"},{"x":1.963,"y":1.963,"z":8.118,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":8.118,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.927,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.927,"z":8.118,"el":"N"},{"x":3.927,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":3.927,"y":0.0,"z":8.118,"el":"N"},{"x":3.927,"y":3.927,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":3.927,"y":3.927,"z":8.118,"el":"N"},{"x":1.963,"y":0.0,"z":6.089,"el":"Ag"},{"x":1.963,"y":3.927,"z":6.089,"el":"Ag"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.963,"z":6.089,"el